  "source_bibliography": [
    {
      "subentry": "O1203002",
      "entry": {
        "TITLE": [
          "A precision measurements of pp elastic scattering cross\nsections at intermediate energies."
        ],
        "REFERENCE": [
          "(J,EPJ/A,22,125,2004)\n(J,PRL,78,1652,1997) Preliminary results.\n(J,NP/A,631,426,1998) same data"
        ],
        "AUTHOR": [
          "(D.Albers, F.Bauer, J.Bisplinghoff, R.Bollmann,\nK.Buesser, M.Busch, R.Daniel, O.Diehl, F.Dohrmann,\nH.P.Engelhardt, J.Ernst, P.D.Eversheim, M.Gasthuber,\nR.Gebel, J.Greiff, A.Gross, R.Gross-Hardt, S.Heider,\nA.Heine, F.Hinterberger, T.Hueskes, M.Igelbrink,\nM.Jeske, R.Langkau, J.Lindlein, R.Maier, R.Maschuw,\nF.Mosel, D.Prasuhn, H.Rohdjess, D.Rosendaal,\nP.von Rossen, N.Scheid, N.Schirm, M.Schulz-Rojahn,\nF.Schwandt, V.Schwarz, W.Scobel, S.Thomas,H.-J.Trelle,\nE.Weise, A.Wellinghausen, K.Woller, R.Ziegler,\nEDDA Collaboration)"
        ],
        "REL-REF": [
          "(R,C0083001,A.J.Simon+,J,PR/C,48,662,1993) The absolute\ncross-section scale was fixed at the reference momentum\n1.455 Gev/c to the high-precision data.\n(R,,R.A.Arndt+,J,PR/C,50,2731,1994) Phase shift\nsolution SM94.\n(R,,R.A.Arndt+,J,PR/C,56,3005,1997) Phase shift\nsolution SM97.\n(R,,R.A.Arndt+,J,PR/C,62,34005,2000) Phase shift\nsolution FA00."
        ],
        "COMMENT": [
          "-By authors. Including the data of the present work\nwill not only slightly modify the phase shifts to\nreflect the differences to previous results but may\nalso allow to improve the ansatz for the variation of\nthe phase shift parameters with energy."
        ],
        "INSTITUTE": [
          "(2GERBON) Helmholtz-Institute.\n(2GERHAM) Institut fuer Experimentalphysik.\n(2GERJUL) Institut fuer Kernphysik."
        ],
        "SAMPLE": [
          "Thin CH(2) fiber targets, thickness 5-mu-m, were used."
        ],
        "ADD-RES": [
          "(COMP) Phase shift solutions Sm94, Sm97, Fa00."
        ],
        "DETECTOR": [
          "(SPEC) The EDDA detector. It consists of scintillator\nbars and rings designed to measure the points, at which\nthe scattered proton and its recoil partner traverse\nthe hodoscope.  The kinematic relationship between\nthese angles are used to identify elastic scattering\nevents. Additional details see in original paper."
        ],
        "FACILITY": [
          "(SYNCH,2GERJUL) The proton synchrotron COSY"
        ],
        "METHOD": [
          "(INTB)\n(COINC) All details in original paper."
        ],
        "ERR-ANALYS": [
          "(ERR-S).The errors that are uncorrelated for each\ndata point, this is given in the column statistical\nthis encompasses the purely statistical error from the\npp scattering yield, the error due to subtraction of\nP-carbon scattering and errors introduced by angle-\nreconstruction and cuts applied in the data analysis.\n(ERR-1).The systematic errors which will be functions\nsmoothly varying with beam momentum and scattering\nangle. This comprises the uncertainty on the overall\ndetection efficiency for pp elastic scattering and the\nuncertainty on possible contaminations from pp-\ninelastic  reactions.\n(ERR-T).The total error is the quadratic sum of ERR-S\nand ERR-1.\nAll data do not contain two types of normalization\nuncertainties:  an overall normalization error of the\nwhole data set of less 1.5% due to the absolute\nnormalization at beam momentum 1455 MeV/c. There is an\nAdditional systematic uncertainty due to the relative\nnormalization of 2.5% common to all data points at the\nsame energy. This error does not apply at the\nnormalization point at 1455 MeV/c. The relative\nnormalization uncertainties at different beam momenta\nare uncorrelated. This is a conservative upper limit\nespecially for beam momenta close to 1455 MeV/c."
        ],
        "STATUS": [
          "(TABLE) The data (more than represent on figures in\npaper) were received from authors."
        ],
        "HISTORY": [
          "(20041110C)\n(20041215A) Correction\n(20041104R) Data tables from the authors.\n(20101209A) New Reference was added.\n(20120611U) SD: Author (EDDA Collaboration) was added."
        ]
      },
      "subentry_bib": {
        "REACTION": [
          "(1-H-1(P,EL)1-H-1,,DA)"
        ]
      }
